@page "/referrals-public"
@page "/referrals"
@page "/early-adoption-incentive"
@layout PublicLayout
@attribute [AllowAnonymous]

<PageTitle>EMA’s Referral Program - Email Money App</PageTitle>

<section class="brochure-information-page referrals-public-page">
    <p class="referrals-intro">
        The EMA Referral Program allows nonprofits and community organizations to share EMA with peers.
        When a referred organization begins using EMA and completes its first monthly billing cycle, both
        organizations receive a credit. The program is designed to encourage collaboration among community
        organizations while keeping the process respectful, simple, and privacy-first.
    </p>

    <div class="referrals-section">
        <h3>1. Program Overview</h3>
        <dl class="referrals-def-list">
            <div class="referrals-def-item">
                <dt>Eligibility to Refer</dt>
                <dd>
                    Organizations may participate in the referral program once they have used EMA for at least
                    14 days and have processed donations during that period.
                </dd>
            </div>

            <div class="referrals-def-item">
                <dt>Permission-Based Referrals</dt>
                <dd>
                    Referrals must be made only after the referring organization has spoken with the prospective
                    organization and received permission to share its contact information with EMA. This ensures
                    that all referrals are welcome and non-intrusive.
                </dd>
            </div>

            <div class="referrals-def-item">
                <dt>Mutual Credit Benefit</dt>
                <dd>
                    When a referred organization completes its first monthly billing cycle, EMA issues a credit to
                    both organizations. The credit amount is equal to the lower of the two invoices for that month.
                    <div class="referrals-example-box">
                        <strong>Example:</strong> If one organization’s invoice is $50 and the other’s is $30, both organizations receive a $30 credit.
                    </div>
                </dd>
            </div>

            <div class="referrals-def-item">
                <dt>Unlimited Participation</dt>
                <dd>
                    Organizations may submit an unlimited number of referrals. Credits may be accumulated and applied
                    to future invoices. Permission is required for each referral.
                </dd>
            </div>
        </dl>
    </div>

    <div class="referrals-section">
        <h3>2. Simple, Secure &amp; Low-Pressure</h3>
        <dl class="referrals-def-list">
            <div class="referrals-def-item">
                <dt>No Direct Marketing</dt>
                <dd>
                    Contact information provided through the referral program is used solely for the referral email.
                    EMA does not use referral information for marketing or outreach.
                </dd>
            </div>

            <div class="referrals-def-item">
                <dt>Privacy-First Approach</dt>
                <dd>
                    EMA does not publish phone numbers, email addresses, or other sensitive contact details.
                </dd>
            </div>

            <div class="referrals-def-item">
                <dt>Independent Evaluation</dt>
                <dd>
                    Prospective organizations may explore EMA at their own pace and verify experiences through their
                    own networks. You can start with a sandbox that requires no email or phone number to try for 30 days.
                </dd>
            </div>
        </dl>
    </div>

    <div class="referrals-section">
        <h3>3. Participating Nonprofit Opt-In Directory</h3>
        <p>
            Some organizations prefer to be publicly visible as active EMA users, while others choose to remain
            private. The ticker tape below supports both preferences.
        </p>

        <dl class="referrals-def-list">
            <div class="referrals-def-item">
                <dt>Opt-In Visibility</dt>
                <dd>
                    An organization may appear in the directory only if it has:
                    <ul>
                        <li>Provided permission for EMA to display its name or logo</li>
                        <li>Processed donations within the past 30 days</li>
                    </ul>
                </dd>
            </div>

            <div class="referrals-def-item">
                <dt>Flexible Control</dt>
                <dd>
                    Organizations may request updates or removal from the directory at any time.
                </dd>
            </div>

            <div class="referrals-def-item">
                <dt>Purpose of the Directory</dt>
                <dd>
                    The directory serves as a simple indicator of organizations currently using EMA and comfortable
                    being publicly identified as users. It is not intended as a channel for outreach or contact.
                </dd>
            </div>
        </dl>

        <!-- Stakeholder Opt-In Directory Ticker Banner (Image Asset) -->
        <div class="ticker-carousel-container" aria-label="Participating Organizations Directory">
            <div class="ticker-carousel-track">
                <img src="/images/referrals-directory-ticker.png"
                     alt="Participating Canadian Organizations - Rated 4.8 Supporting Canadian Nonprofits and Businesses"
                     class="ticker-carousel-image" />
                <img src="/images/referrals-directory-ticker.png"
                     alt=""
                     aria-hidden="true"
                     class="ticker-carousel-image" />
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>
